{#- The card heading is the source name (main.py imposes it), so the article
    title belongs here: without it the card says only which feed spoke. What the
    heading does already carry is the source, which is why the "Source:" line is
    gone. Summaries are capped at 1500 characters upstream, a wall of text in a
    card; 400 is an excerpt that invites the click. CVE ids and the date ride on
    one line so the reader can judge relevance before opening anything. -#}
**{{ title }}**
{% if cves %}
{{ cves | join(' · ') }}{% if published %} · {{ published }}{% endif %}
{% elif published %}
{{ published }}
{% endif %}
{%- if summary %}

{{ summary | truncate(400, false, ' […]') }}
{% endif %}
{%- if url %}

[Read the full item]({{ url }})
{%- endif %}
